Z||000000||NEPTUNE||12-20-2001||10:16 AM||||I wish I had a dollar for every time i've heard that!<BR>Todays Orlando Sentinel published a list of current recalls:<BR>"BMW:<BR> The automaker is recalling 22,000 2001 3 series cars, Z8S and XS Spurt Utilities because of a faulty radiator cooling fan switch may cause fires.<BR>Daimler Chrysler: <BR>..is recalling 98,000 200-201 Dodge Ram vans to inspect a power seat connector that could fail, causing a fire.<BR>Ford Motor Co.:<BR>..is recalling 1.7MILLION 200-201 Focus, Taurus, Expedition and F series pickups, and 200-2001 Lincoln Town Car, Navigator and Continental, and 200-2001 Mercury Sable vehicles to inspect an underhood switch for the windshield wipers that could fail and start a fire.<BR>Mitsubishi:<BR>is recalling 26,000 2000 Gallants and Eclipses because an exhaust manifold heat shield could come in contact with a power steering fluid line, resukting in, you guessed it, FIRE!   <BR>I wonder how many of THESE vehicles will still be on the road in fifteen years....<p>[This message has been edited by NEPTUNE (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||4
