Z||000002||Fformula88||12-20-2001||10:33 AM||||It depends on where footage of the car burning up shows up.  If the automaker has found a potential fault that could cause a Fier, they could issue a recall.  It doesn't mean they have started burning up in mass quantities.<P>Any car has the potential to start on Fire.  <P>Fiero's have the reputation because they were starting on Fire because of a fault, and it wasn't just one or two cars.  I know its a touchy topic here, but they were burning back in the day, and it was made well known by the media at the time.  Now if Bimmers start burning up and the news gets some footage, everyone is gonna think 3 series cars are fire prone too.  <BR>||||reg||1
